      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Natural Vegetation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tropical Deciduous Forests are the most widespread vegetation type in India, often called Monsoon Forests.",
        "Tropical Evergreen Forests thrive in regions with over 200 cm of annual rainfall, maintaining lush green canopy year-round.",
        "Thorn Forests occur in arid and semi-arid regions with less than 50 cm of rainfall, featuring acacias, palms, and cacti.",
        "Mountain Forests show altitudinal zonation of vegetation ranging from wet temperate to alpine grasslands.",
        "Mangrove Forests flourish in coastal deltaic regions influenced by tides, dominated by species like Sundari trees."
      ],
      "id": "ia40zsx"
